cadtui localisation — keyboard-alias probe from .pgp (P3, CI/runner)

Parent: cadtui.issue (Phase 7). Harvest the keyboard command aliases (the third,
distinct dictionary) from the CAD install's alias file — acad.pgp / default.pgp
(spec lines ~674-677, ~756-758). These are purely LOCAL and are NEVER
`_`-prefixed; keep them strictly apart from the command-name dictionary
(cadtui-locale-probe-getcname).

What to collect
- The (alias . command) pairs from the shipped .pgp / .pgp-equivalent of each
  localised install.

How
- Simplest: read the .pgp from the install as a probe-job artifact (it is a data
  file; no CAD scripting needed beyond locating it). Mirror the soft cad-tagged
  job pattern in .gitlab/native.yml; emit under dist/pgp/. May be foldable into
  the getcname probe job's artifact collection.

Matrix
- Per vendor × locale × platform, aligned with the getcname probe.

Output feeds cadtui-locale-data-format-and-loader.issue (aliases.sexp).
